nodecode-ai-visibility is a rewrite of meelis545's meelis545/qqq-ai-visibility-mcp:
  https://github.com/meelis545/qqq-ai-visibility-mcp
  commit 06278fa89aef5ad40605722f494b069905f62732
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 QQQ OÜ (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin carries no code of its own -- a portable manifest that
points a harness at the hosted MCP server https://qqq.ee/mcp -- so what is
rewritten is the conversation with that server. One JSON-RPC 2.0 tools/call
per check, POSTed with the headers a Streamable HTTP server expects, its
answer read either as one JSON object or as server-sent events, and the text
the server writes for the person returned whole: the crawler and readiness
checks of check_ai_visibility, the stored brand-mention and citation report
of get_public_report, and the tool description of get_tool_info. The domain
and language arguments, the en/et pair, the bare-domain normalisation and
the rule that the result text is shown as it came, links included, follow
the original's skill. The original's three tool names are kept as the three
tool names here.

Left out: the Hermes skills/ and clawhub/ folders as files -- their guidance
is the help topic and the tool descriptions. Also left out: the MCP session
handshake (initialize and the Mcp-Session-Id header), which the original's
own documented curl calls skip as well; a server that starts to require one
is a Gaps entry, not a silent retry. And the plugin's per-client config
files for other harnesses, which say nothing a cell can use.
